# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
import lib/cadkernel/arc_fit2.dl
function fit2 check {boolean:condition}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 81)

set points to a list containing (the cad zero vector2)
append (a cad vector2 with x 3 and y 4) to points
set directions to a list containing (an automatic cad arc fit direction2)
append (an automatic cad arc fit direction2) to directions
set fitted to the cad arc chain2 through points with closure false and directions directions
fit2 check fitted's valid
fit2 check ((the length of fitted's vertices) = 2)
set first to the item at 0 in fitted's vertices
set last to the item at 1 in fitted's vertices
fit2 check (((first's point's x = 0.0) and (first's point's y = 0.0)) and (first's bulge = 0.0))
fit2 check ((last's point's x = 3.0) and (last's point's y = 4.0))
print "two_points_remain_one_straight_span" as a line

clear points
append (the cad zero vector2) to points
append (a cad vector2 with x 1 and y 1) to points
append (a cad vector2 with x 2 and y 0) to points
append (an automatic cad arc fit direction2) to directions
set fitted to the cad arc chain2 through points with closure false and directions directions
fit2 check fitted's valid
set first to the item at 0 in fitted's vertices
set last to the item at ((the length of fitted's vertices) - 1) in fitted's vertices
fit2 check ((first's point's x = 0.0) and (first's point's y = 0.0))
fit2 check ((last's point's x = 2.0) and (last's point's y = 0.0))
loop index from 0 to the length of fitted's vertices:
    set vertex to the item at index in fitted's vertices
    fit2 check (((the absolute value of vertex's point's x) <= 1.7976931348623157e308) and ((the absolute value of vertex's point's y) <= 1.7976931348623157e308))
    fit2 check (((the absolute value of vertex's bulge) <= 1.7976931348623157e308) and ((the absolute value of vertex's fraction) <= 1.7976931348623157e308))
print "curved_chain_keeps_endpoints_and_returns_finite_arcs" as a line

replace item at index 0 in directions with (a cad arc fit direction2 along (a cad vector2 with x 1.7976931348623157e308 and y 1.7976931348623157e308))
set fitted to the cad arc chain2 through points with closure false and directions directions
fit2 check (fitted's valid = false)
fit2 check ((the length of fitted's vertices) = 0)
free points
free directions
print "invalid_direction_rejects_the_entire_fit" as a line

